WEBVTT

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.900
I shouldn't have lost that bet.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.190
Appare, you're a maniac!

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:19.980
Winning with an implausible plan,
they secured the storehouse and car.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.610
But it's nothing more than
a prelude to the long, cruel race.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.570
Kosame. Table five.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.650
Coming right up!

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.440
Clean up table one!

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.980
Episode 5:
Let It Go

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.280
Got it!

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.280
Excuse me!

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:05.530
I'm coming!

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.280
Hey! Coffee!

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.900
With pleasure!

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.610
I wish I had a car.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.070
They're super expensive, you dope.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:17.070
We could work for ten years and not afford one.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:22.530
That's it! If I sold the car,
wouldn't that pay for the fare to Japan?!

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.150
H-Hey!

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.780
We don't have to enter the race!

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.730
Appare might not like it,
but half of that car belongs to me!

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.190
I touched the finish line!

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:40.070
Japan! I'm coming home!

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.860
Hey, Appare! About the car...!

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.190
Yeah? I just disassembled it.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:55.150
Huh? I thought I heard Kosame here.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:58.030
Yeah. He went back to work.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.070
What'd he even come for?

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.570
Beats me.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:04.610
More importantly, I had a great idea.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:05.570
Hmm?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:07.820
Three months till the race...

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:13.280
My machine will devour the parts of Al's car...

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.940
...and give birth to a new one.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:19.070
Say what? You want to be tested?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:19.900
Yes.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.730
I told you--women can't be racers.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:26.480
You're wrong! I know it's wrong...

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.780
Test me! I'll prove that it's possible!

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.730
Not happening. This ain't a school.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:37.570
You don't get to have a go
just 'cuz you raised your hand.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.440
It'll be a good laugh, Owner. Wear this.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:46.730
Quit it, David. The machines aren't toys.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.480
Just let her putter around the course.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.900
She'll get the point and keep her mouth shut.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.030
If she can get that far!

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:57.610
Here ya go.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:00.110
Clean it for me when you're done.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:03.110
Now that's a job fit for a woman.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.730
Ow!

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.650
You're asking for it!

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:13.110
Ow! Ow, ow, ow!

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.110
Jing, quit it!

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:16.730
He's the one who insulted me and my job first!

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.730
You wanna get fired?!

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.400
Shit!

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.280
Apologize to David.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.780
Fine.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:33.570
If he's your idea of
an ideal racer, then fire me.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:34.570
Hmm?

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.440
But before you do, let me race him!

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.570
What?!

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.360
Should I hit you instead?

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:41.380
Say what?!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.110
Enough! Quit it!

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:46.400
If it means so much, we'll have a race.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.690
Thirty minutes before practice on Wednesday.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:52.690
But, Jing... You get Number 0.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:53.530
Huh?

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:55.440
That hunk of junk?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.440
I won't let some amateur drive any car of value.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.690
Right...

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:06.400
Let the mechanics know: If you wanna
work on 0, do it on your own time.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.190
This race ain't costing me a dime.

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:15.230
As for you, Jing... When the race is over,
take your stuff and leave.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.900
Are we clear?

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.230
Yeah.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.690
Quit yawning. You'll scare the fish.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.320
As if there's any here.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.610
Huh?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.230
Switch spots with me.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:41.940
The spot doesn't matter.
You've just gotta be smarter than a fish.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.230
What are you saying?

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.320
Huh?

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.230
Xialian?

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:56.110
Xialian! What are you doing?!

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.690
Huh?

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.610
Kosame! Is Appare around?

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:12.070
Hey, Appare!

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.360
Appare?!

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.360
Meal time?

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:15.980
Not yet. It's actually--

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.150
Don't bug me unless it's food.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.480
Wha...?! Hey!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.650
Appare!

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.360
Hmm? Oh... What's up?

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.280
Appare, I need a favor.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.530
So this is Number 0?

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:34.610
That's right. They don't
race it 'cuz it acts up.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:39.360
In fact, the engine even stopped
on the way here, so I pushed it.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.190
And your mechanics?

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:46.320
I made enemies of David,
so none of 'em will work on it for free.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.900
So heartless.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:53.480
No, it's only natural.
He's the official driver of the team.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.780
Okay. Leave it to me.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.030
I'll give it an emergency acceleration--

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.320
--Don't do it!
--Please, don't!

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.030
I just want it serviced to race!

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:04.400
Wha...?

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:08.980
Please! It's pointless
if I win because of the car!

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:11.070
Even if it seems unfair,

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:15.400
unless I win using skill,
it won't be like I beat him!

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.440
Boring.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.190
Don't say that, Appare.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.860
You could've entered the race
using the car from Al,

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:25.280
yet aren't you insisting on building your own?

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:31.610
All right. If it just needs
servicing, let <i>him</i> do it.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:32.820
Pardon!

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.070
Hello!

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.730
Wha...?! Huh!

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:38.440
Hello!

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:47.230
I get the picture, but why did you
come to me to service the car?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.360
She's in a hurry.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.030
And we can't pay.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:53.820
It's almost comical how brazen you guys are.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:58.070
However, this lets us see
the handiwork of another maker.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:03.900
And if all it needs is a quick fix
for one race, that's easy enough.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:04.860
Then...?

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.190
We'll do it.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:09.150
Thank you! I'll stay here and help!

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:14.820
Still, even if it's fixed,
winning a race is no easy feat.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.440
No worries! Her driving is the real deal!

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:21.650
A race is nothing like driving alone.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:26.440
There's fights for the racing line,
turbulence from dirty air...

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:30.980
You can't do as you please
like when driving alone.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:35.570
Racing is a dangerous and dirty world.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.690
I'll fit right in.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:38.650
All right.

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:43.900
But what will you do if you
win the race and still get fired?

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.030
Well...

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:48.610
I'm not thinking about the future.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.320
I'm fighting to defend my pride.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.780
I'm out. Gotta finish my own car.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:56.640
Excuse us...

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.730
Think it'll turn out good?

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:03.230
Yeah, it'll amaze you. You, and the world.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.480
Will it be done before the race?

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.940
Well... I'm not thinking about it.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.690
You should be!

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.860
The race is ten laps.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.900
Hey, what's the consensus?

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.190
Everyone's betting on three.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:28.110
It's the number of laps
you'll do before I go ten.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:30.820
Ten laps!

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.070
All this on ten!

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:37.530
Hey! This area is off-limits to--

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:39.570
Hey, what's that car?!

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:51.440
Isn't that BNW's Al Lyon?!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.030
I came to spectate.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.780
Sofia, could you prepare the tea?

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:01.610
Sure.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.480
What a grand entrance.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:06.440
Yeah? Yours is just too plain.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.780
Would you all like some tea?

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:10.900
Oh, you're so kind.

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:11.940
Where's Appare?

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:16.900
I invited him, but he just doesn't
listen when he's working.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:18.650
I see.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:22.860
Whatever... Hey! Get on with it!

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:32.900
Lemme give you some advice.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:36.650
It's gas on the right and brakes on the left.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:39.280
Shove it.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.360
What would you do?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:01.280
How do you beat someone with a better engine?

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:11.480
Hey, Appare. You hear me?

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:14.650
I'm driving right now. Don't talk.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.030
Driving?

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:21.650
I don't have time to make a prototype,
so I'm driving it in my head.

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:41.280
Surfaces... Temperature... Weather...

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:48.570
I'm driving it through
all conditions, revising as I go.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.530
Yeah?

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:14.650
A car's speed isn't determined
by the engine alone.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:20.570
There's aerodynamics, weight,
tire condition, fuel amount and quality...

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:21.940
True...

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:27.150
If you can't win against their engine,
win with something else.

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:33.360
I've got this. I came here to win.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:38.900
She's fast!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.070
What?!

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.320
Yes! She won!

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.110
The race has only just begun.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:58.400
Hmph! She only got a better start
'cuz women are lighter.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:01.320
But that's not enough to win.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.280
Her engine seems a little less powerful.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:20.570
Shit!

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:24.610
Kosame... Watch your language,
there's children here.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.730
Oops, sorry...

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.860
Where's the "don't treat me like a child"?

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:33.360
Sofia's an exception.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.860
Yeah! Pass 'em!

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:59.110
No... She's barely able to keep up.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:04.400
If a more powerful car pulls ahead
even once, it's bad news.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.400
She can't make a mistake.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:24.070
Enjoy the view of my ass till the finish line!

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.610
David isn't pulling away...

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:35.820
But he won't get passed!

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:41.360
Yeah! Just two more! Keep the lead!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.530
You fools.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:43.360
Huh?

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:46.900
David hasn't taken the lead--
she's giving it to him.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:47.820
What?

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.480
If she sticks that close to him,

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:54.230
the low air pressure makes up for her engine.

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:56.730
It preserves tire grip, too.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:02.900
That's not all. Better fuel efficiency
lets her use less and weigh less.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:05.110
That explains the good start!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:09.360
Just wait! She's wagering it all
on the last corner!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.900
It's a break battle!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:28.530
Don't chicken out! Show her
what men are made of, David!

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.230
Yeah!

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:38.730
Just pass her up!

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.070
No, he can't.

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:40.980
Huh?

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:47.190
David wore out his tires by panicking
and driving aggressively at the start.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:49.320
His tires are at their limit.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:51.320
Shit! Get back here!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.780
The final corner!

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:05.440
Yeah! She's leading!

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.320
Coward!

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:27.690
Xialian!

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:32.360
You okay?!

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:36.110
Wha...? Hey...

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:52.360
I won! You see that?!

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.610
What the hell was that all about?!

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.820
Amateurs like you don't get to--

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.360
What kind of racer are you?!

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:05.610
If you caused a crash,
I would've fired your ass!

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:12.070
All right, playtime is over!
Everyone, back to work!

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:15.780
Ow, ow, ow...

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:22.860
By winning, I wanted to prove
I could do it, too...

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.690
Is this... the end for me?

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:28.940
You fool.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:35.150
When you spun, any normal person
would've slammed on the brakes.

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:38.940
But if you did, you would've hit the wall.

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:45.030
Instead, you stepped on the gas
and got the car back under control.

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:48.940
It takes a real racer to do that.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.480
Owner...

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:56.900
Thing is, Jing... People come here
to watch a fierce battle between men.

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:59.940
They see themselves as the racer.

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:02.480
Almost no women come watch.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:08.940
So, nobody here will be cheering for you
or be happy if a woman wins.

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:13.530
But I think I'll lend you Number 0.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:14.690
Huh?

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:18.110
Don't you wanna enter the Trans-America race?

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:23.690
It might be tough to
cross the country in that car,

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:30.530
but if you're leading the race at the first
supply point, society might acknowledge it--

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:34.570
that women can have the spirit of a racer, too.

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:36.570
Right!

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:38.440
Good for you, Xialian!

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:43.610
All things being equal,
you'd be a good rival as a racer.

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:45.690
Jing, we're sorry.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:50.690
If you can forgive us,
could you let us work on Number 0?

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:55.190
We'll turn it into something
that can take you cross-country!

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.400
Owner!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:19:02.980
Suit yourself. But if you win anything,
you owe me some for their wages.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.730
Guys...

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.860
Yeah! Please do!

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.760
"B.I.G. BOSS'S IRON MOTOR COMPANY HIRES
TJ FROM 'THOUSAND THREE' AS DRIVER!"

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:21.110
To think Iron Motor would hire TJ,
one of the Thousand Three, as a driver...

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:24.570
TJ, huh? What a scumbag.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:27.610
Is he an acquaintance of yours, Mr. Oldin?

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:29.190
Kinda.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:37.150
Not exactly by choice.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:42.900
Everyone has heard of the legendary outlaws,
the Thousand Three...

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:47.690
Dylan the Hero, Crazy TJ, and Gil the Butcher.

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:50.150
I'm no hero.

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:54.900
You were pardoned for your deeds in war.

00:19:54.900 --> 00:20:00.320
However, the other two have bounties
of over $50,000 for their heads.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:05.320
Upon the request of B.I.G BOSS,
the police have agreed not to interfere...

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:09.150
...and will allow them to race until it's over.

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:12.360
You think the police will keep their promise?

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:19.230
Rumor has it that Gil the Butcher
has entered for the prize money, too.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:24.150
This race... While it raises the curtain
on the era of automobiles,

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:32.820
it's also a competition of the B.I.G. BOSS
sponsors: BNW, Iron, and us at GM.

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:35.070
Losing is unacceptable.

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:39.190
Not that I care. Still, I don't intend to lose.

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:45.820
I'm counting on you. If we win this race,
I'll be a GM executive in no time.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:49.480
Hmph... Keep some booze for me
at the finish line.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:52.780
How does 30-year-old Camus sound?

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.610
Not bad.

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:56.070
Here.

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:58.730
Send it to the usual place.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.030
Right.

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:13.030
There's no way in hell I'll go back
to being a filthy engineer.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:21.070
Have anything to say as B.I.G. BOSS's
sole European power?

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:24.860
It won't be Europe or America,
but me who wins it.

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:26.820
"BNW SCION AL LYON BOLDLY DECLARES WAR!"

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:29.320
"DYLAN THE HERO, THE MAN NEAREST TO
WINNING THE MILLION, CONTINUES HIS SILENCE."

00:21:30.610 --> 00:21:32.070
"THE TRANS-AMERICA RACE'S SOLE FEMALE RACER
SHOULDERS THE EXPECTATIONS OF HER COMRADES."

00:21:32.110 --> 00:21:33.320
"CRAZY TJ GOES ON RAMPAGE BEFORE THE RACE!"

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:34.570
"THE MYSTERY MAN,
GIL OF THE THOUSAND THREE, APPEARS!"

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:35.570
"TALENTED RACERS ASSEMBLE TO CHALLENGE B.I.G. BOSS!"

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:36.570
"BRAVE MEN LOOKING TO TURN THEIR LIVES AROUND JOIN AS RACERS!"

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:44.360
Hey, Appare! The newspaper people are coming!

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:47.030
Don't you wanna be in the photo?

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.440
Shut up. I don't care.

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:54.900
Then as representative of Team Kosame,
I'll do the interview and--

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:55.860
Get it?

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:56.780
Yup.

00:21:56.780 --> 00:21:58.280
M'kay, let's go.

00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:01.230
Huh? Um, the interview...?

00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:04.150
We don't have time for everyone's story.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:07.730
A photo's more than you small fry deserve.

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:12.150
Appare! You better finish that!

00:22:12.150 --> 00:22:16.570
We've gotta win the race
and make the front page!

00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:19.570
I know. It's almost done.

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:47.480
Next time

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:49.990
Episode 5: The Eve, and...
